  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of comprehensive, quality life-saving&#xa0;GBV response and prevention among the most vulnerable population affected by the 2023 crisis in Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main goal of this project is to provide multi-sectorial and integrated Gender-Based Violence (GBV) and Sexual and Reproductive Health (SRH) response services to vulnerable people affected by conflict. This UNFPA provides mobile clinic services and psychological support to GBV survivors, as well as procures and distributes reproductive health kits. This project supports a total of 88,847 people, of whom 61% are women, 31% are children, and 8% are men. 4,442 people with disabilities are also supported.</narrative>
  </description>
